  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is a flat rate of 6% on the value of the estate exceeding Five Million Pesos (₱5,000,000).\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 84 of the NIRC specifies that the estate tax is imposed on the transfer of the net estate of a decedent. The flat rate of 6% applies only to the portion of the estate that exceeds the threshold of ₱5,000,000. This means that estates valued at or below this threshold are exempt from estate tax.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor estate planning and administration, this means that executors and heirs must assess the total value of the estate to determine if it exceeds the ₱5,000,000 threshold. If it does, they will need to calculate the estate tax based on the excess amount at the 6% rate. This simplification of the estate tax structure under TRAIN aims to ease the tax burden on smaller estates while ensuring that larger estates contribute fairly to government revenues.",
